From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(init): a failed generator does not pass the check with
 the old configuration
Requires: 008-check-config-before-stop 019-missing-rule-sets

check_new_config() (patch 008) ran the generator without looking at its
exit code and kept the previous sing-box-c.json / sing-box-s.json in
place while it ran. A generator that stops before it writes the new file
(die() for a node that is missing, exit(1) of generate_server.uc) left
the old file, "sing-box check" passed on it, and reload or restart went
on as if the new settings were applied: they were not, and the log said
nothing.

The previous file is now moved to .bak before the generator runs (it was
copied there), and the check needs the generator to exit with 0 and the
new file to exist. On a failure the old file comes back from .bak, as
before, and the running service is kept.

Checked: check_new_config() of the patched init script under busybox ash
with a stub generator and sing-box: old file and a generator that dies -
before: the check passed on the old file, now: it fails and the old file
is restored; a new valid file, a new invalid file, no old file - as
before.

diff --git a/root/etc/init.d/homeproxy b/root/etc/init.d/homeproxy
index a3a03a3..1988e1d 100755
--- a/root/etc/init.d/homeproxy
+++ b/root/etc/init.d/homeproxy
@@ -498,11 +498,13 @@ check_new_config() {
 		fi
 
 		rm -f "$RUN_DIR/sing-box-$name.json.bak"
+		# The previous file is moved away: a generator that fails before it
+		# writes the new one must not leave the old one to pass the check.
 		[ ! -e "$RUN_DIR/sing-box-$name.json" ] || \
-			cp -p "$RUN_DIR/sing-box-$name.json" "$RUN_DIR/sing-box-$name.json.bak"
+			mv -f "$RUN_DIR/sing-box-$name.json" "$RUN_DIR/sing-box-$name.json.bak"
 		generated="$generated $name"
-		ucode -S "$HP_DIR/scripts/$gen" 2>>"$LOG_PATH"
-		if [ -e "$RUN_DIR/sing-box-$name.json" ] && \
+		if ucode -S "$HP_DIR/scripts/$gen" 2>>"$LOG_PATH" && \
+		   [ -e "$RUN_DIR/sing-box-$name.json" ] && \
 		   "$PROG" --disable-color check --config "$RUN_DIR/sing-box-$name.json" 2>>"$LOG_PATH"; then
 			cp -p "$RUN_DIR/sing-box-$name.json" "$RUN_DIR/sing-box-$name.json.checked"
 		else
